  "notes": "{金|かね} is the everyday, somewhat casual word for money.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {金|かね}がある/ない (to have/not have money)\n- {金|かね}を{使|つか}う (to spend money)\n- {金|かね}を{貯|た}める (to save money)\n- {金|かね}を{払|はら}う (to pay money)\n- {金|かね}を{借|か}りる (to borrow money)\n\nCOMPOUND WORDS:\n- お{金|かね} (money - polite form)\n- {金持|かねも}ち (rich person)\n- {金|かね}づかい (spending habits)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {金|かね}/お{金|かね}: money (everyday)\n- {現金|げんきん}: cash (as opposed to card)\n- {資金|しきん}: funds, capital (business)\n\nNOTE: お{金|かね} with the お prefix is more polite and commonly used.",
